-- Execution requires a witnessed whole-observation call and its bound input.
-- Naming an operation is semantic evidence; it does not establish a request.
\set ECHO none
NOTICE:  operational memory: aliases do not invoke; active context and sourced call/input execute current state; incompatible evidence is rejected
NOTICE:  operational memory: each declared input retains its own completion obligation
NOTICE:  operational memory: an admitted relation executes without compiled lexical names
NOTICE:  operational memory: distinct Unicode surfaces execute the same canonical semantic input and operation
NOTICE:  operational memory: canonical inputs sharing one surface retain separate completion obligations
NOTICE:  operational memory: distinct semantic inputs remain ambiguous even when their surface occurrence is shared
NOTICE:  operational memory: native parse roles bind exact ordered occurrences; quoted, reordered and refuted annotations cannot supply inputs
